{"name":"Rosario Ridge","hex":"#d9bebb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ridge","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The back of any animal; especially the upper or projecting part of the back of a quadruped.","Any extended protuberance; a projecting line or strip."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form into a ridge.","To extend in ridges."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ridge"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rosario","blocks":[{"text":"Rosario, officially the Autonomous City of Rosario, is a city in central Argentina, in the south of the province of Santa Fe. Located 300 km (186 mi) northwest of Buenos Aires on the west bank of the Paraná River, it is the country's third-most populous city after Buenos Aires and Córdoba. With a growing and important metropolitan area, Greater Rosario has an estimated population of 1,750,000 as of 2020. One of its main attractions includes the neoclassical, Art Nouveau, and Art Deco architecture that has been preserved in hundreds of residences, houses and public buildings. The city is also famous for being the birthplace of revolutionary Marxist Che Guevara and footballer Lionel Messi."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/J30_869_Rosario.jpg/330px-J30_869_Rosario.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosario"},{"title":"Ridge","blocks":[{"text":"A ridge is a long, narrow, elevated geomorphologic landform, structural feature, or a combination of both separated from the surrounding terrain by steep sides. The sides of a ridge slope away from a narrow top, the crest or ridgecrest, with the terrain dropping down on either side. The crest, if narrow, is also called a ridgeline. Limitations on the dimensions of a ridge are lacking. Its height above the surrounding terrain can vary from less than a meter to hundreds of meters. A ridge can be either depositional, erosional, tectonic, or a combination of these in origin and can consist of either bedrock, loose sediment, lava, or ice depending on its origin. A ridge can occur as either an isolated, independent feature or part of a larger geomorphological and/or structural feature. Frequently, a ridge can be further subdivided into smaller geomorphic or structural elements."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/%E4%B8%AD%E6%A9%AB%E5%85%AC%E8%B7%AF%E7%9C%BA%E6%9C%9B%E6%A2%A8%E5%B1%B1%E5%8F%8A%E9%9B%AA%E5%B1%B1%E5%8D%97%E7%A8%9C2.jpg/330px-%E4%B8%AD%E6%A9%AB%E5%85%AC%E8%B7%AF%E7%9C%BA%E6%9C%9B%E6%A2%A8%E5%B1%B1%E5%8F%8A%E9%9B%AA%E5%B1%B1%E5%8D%97%E7%A8%9C2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ridge"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Puente_Rosario_-_Victoria_tomada_desde_un_Villa_Cari%C3%B1o_de_Baigorrina..jpg/500px-Puente_Rosario_-_Victoria_tomada_desde_un_Villa_Cari%C3%B1o_de_Baigorrina..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Puente_Rosario_-_Victoria_tomada_desde_un_Villa_Cari%C3%B1o_de_Baigorrina..jpg/1280px-Puente_Rosario_-_Victoria_tomada_desde_un_Villa_Cari%C3%B1o_de_Baigorrina..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Puente_Rosario_-_Victoria_tomada_desde_un_Villa_Cari%C3%B1o_de_Baigorrina..jpg/500px-Puente_Rosario_-_Victoria_tomada_desde_un_Villa_Cari%C3%B1o_de_Baigorrina..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APuente_Rosario_-_Victoria_tomada_desde_un_Villa_Cari%C3%B1o_de_Baigorrina..jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Bolsa_de_Comercio_Rosario.jpg/500px-Bolsa_de_Comercio_Rosario.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&